Q1. Calculate Total Sales.

DAX:
Total Sales =
SUM(Sales[SalesAmount])


Q2. Calculate Total Profit.

DAX:
Total Profit =
SUM(Sales[Profit])


Q3. Calculate Profit Margin.

DAX:
Profit Margin =
DIVIDE(
    [Total Profit],
    [Total Sales],
    0
)


Q4. Calculate Sales for the Previous Year.

DAX:
Previous Year Sales =
CALCULATE(
    [Total Sales],
    SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR('Date'[Date])
)


Q5. Calculate Year-over-Year Sales Growth.

DAX:
YoY Sales Growth =
VAR CurrentSales = [Total Sales]
VAR PreviousSales = [Previous Year Sales]

RETURN
DIVIDE(
    CurrentSales - PreviousSales,
    PreviousSales,
    0
)
